{"schema_version":"1.8.0","id":"OESA-2026-3248","published":"2026-08-07T02:41:54Z","modified":"2026-08-07T03:00:55.375742136Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-64612"],"summary":"cups-filters security update","details":"This project provides backends, filters, and other software that was once part of the core CUPS distribution but is no longer maintained by Apple Inc. In addition it contains additional filters and software developed independently of Apple, especially filters for the PDF-centric printing workflow introduced by OpenPrinting and a daemon to browse Bonjour broadcasts of remote CUPS printers to make these printers available locally and to provide backward compatibility to the old CUPS broadcasting and browsing of CUPS 1.5.x and older.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA flaw was found in libcupsfilters and cups-filters. The PNG image reading function creates a libpng reader without installing an error recovery handler, causing the CUPS image filter process to abort when processing a malformed PNG file. An unauthenticated attacker could exploit this by submitting a specially crafted PNG print job, leading to denial of service of the in-flight print job.(CVE-2026-64612)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"cups-filters","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP3","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/cups-filters&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.28.15-7.oe2403sp3"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["cups-filters-1.28.15-7.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","cups-filters-debuginfo-1.28.15-7.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","cups-filters-debugsource-1.28.15-7.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","cups-filters-devel-1.28.15-7.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["cups-filters-help-1.28.15-7.oe2403sp3.noarch.rpm"],"src":["cups-filters-1.28.15-7.oe2403sp3.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["cups-filters-1.28.15-7.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","cups-filters-debuginfo-1.28.15-7.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","cups-filters-debugsource-1.28.15-7.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","cups-filters-devel-1.28.15-7.oe24